.TH "MV"  "" "" ""
.SH NAME
mv \- 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
Moves a local file or S3 object to another location locally or in S3.
The \fBmv\fP command copies the source object or file to the specified
destination and then deletes the source object or file.
.sp
\fBWARNING:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If you are using any type of access point ARNs or access point aliases
in your S3 URIs, you must take extra care to make sure that your source
and destination S3 URIs resolve to different underlying buckets. If the
source and destination buckets are the same, the source file or object
can be moved onto itself, which can result in accidental deletion of
your source file or object.
.sp
To verify that the source and destination buckets are not the same,
use the \fB\-\-validate\-same\-s3\-paths\fP parameter, or set the environment
variable \fBAWS_CLI_S3_MV_VALIDATE_SAME_S3_PATHS\fP to \fBtrue\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
  mv
<LocalPath> <S3Uri> or <S3Uri> <LocalPath> or <S3Uri> <S3Uri>
[\-\-dryrun]
[\-\-quiet]
[\-\-include <value>]
[\-\-exclude <value>]
[\-\-acl <value>]
[\-\-follow\-symlinks | \-\-no\-follow\-symlinks]
[\-\-no\-guess\-mime\-type]
[\-\-sse <value>]
[\-\-sse\-c <value>]
[\-\-sse\-c\-key <value>]
[\-\-sse\-kms\-key\-id <value>]
[\-\-sse\-c\-copy\-source <value>]
[\-\-sse\-c\-copy\-source\-key <value>]
[\-\-storage\-class <value>]
[\-\-grants <value> [<value>...]]
[\-\-website\-redirect <value>]
[\-\-content\-type <value>]
[\-\-cache\-control <value>]
[\-\-content\-disposition <value>]
[\-\-content\-encoding <value>]
[\-\-content\-language <value>]
[\-\-expires <value>]
[\-\-source\-region <value>]
[\-\-only\-show\-errors]
[\-\-no\-progress]
[\-\-progress\-frequency <value>]
[\-\-progress\-multiline]
[\-\-page\-size <value>]
[\-\-ignore\-glacier\-warnings]
[\-\-force\-glacier\-transfer]
[\-\-request\-payer <value>]
[\-\-checksum\-mode <value>]
[\-\-checksum\-algorithm <value>]
[\-\-metadata <value>]
[\-\-copy\-props <value>]
[\-\-metadata\-directive <value>]
[\-\-recursive]
[\-\-validate\-same\-s3\-paths]
[\-\-debug]
[\-\-endpoint\-url <value>]
[\-\-no\-verify\-ssl]
[\-\-no\-paginate]
[\-\-output <value>]
[\-\-query <value>]
[\-\-profile <value>]
[\-\-region <value>]
[\-\-version <value>]
[\-\-color <value>]
[\-\-no\-sign\-request]
[\-\-ca\-bundle <value>]
[\-\-cli\-read\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-binary\-format <value>]
[\-\-no\-cli\-pager]
[\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
[\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OPTIONS
.sp
\fBpaths\fP (string)
.sp
\fB\-\-dryrun\fP (boolean)
Displays the operations that would be performed using the specified command without actually running them.
.sp
\fB\-\-quiet\fP (boolean)
Does not display the operations performed from the specified command.
.sp
\fB\-\-include\fP (string)
Don\(aqt exclude files or objects in the command that match the specified pattern. See \fI\%Use of Exclude and Include Filters\fP for details.
.sp
\fB\-\-exclude\fP (string)
Exclude all files or objects from the command that matches the specified pattern.
.sp
\fB\-\-acl\fP (string)
Sets the ACL for the object when the command is performed. If you use this parameter you must have the \(dqs3:PutObjectAcl\(dq permission included in the list of actions for your IAM policy. Only accepts values of \fBprivate\fP, \fBpublic\-read\fP, \fBpublic\-read\-write\fP, \fBauthenticated\-read\fP, \fBaws\-exec\-read\fP, \fBbucket\-owner\-read\fP, \fBbucket\-owner\-full\-control\fP and \fBlog\-delivery\-write\fP\&. See \fI\%Canned ACL\fP for details
.sp
\fB\-\-follow\-symlinks\fP | \fB\-\-no\-follow\-symlinks\fP (boolean)
Symbolic links are followed only when uploading to S3 from the local filesystem. Note that S3 does not support symbolic links, so the contents of the link target are uploaded under the name of the link. When neither \fB\-\-follow\-symlinks\fP nor \fB\-\-no\-follow\-symlinks\fP is specified, the default is to follow symlinks.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-guess\-mime\-type\fP (boolean)
Do not try to guess the mime type for uploaded files. By default the mime type of a file is guessed when it is uploaded.
.sp
\fB\-\-sse\fP (string)
Specifies server\-side encryption of the object in S3. Valid values are \fBAES256\fP and \fBaws:kms\fP\&. If the parameter is specified but no value is provided, \fBAES256\fP is used.
.sp
\fB\-\-sse\-c\fP (string)
Specifies server\-side encryption using customer provided keys of the the object in S3. \fBAES256\fP is the only valid value. If the parameter is specified but no value is provided, \fBAES256\fP is used. If you provide this value, \fB\-\-sse\-c\-key\fP must be specified as well.
.sp
\fB\-\-sse\-c\-key\fP (blob)
The customer\-provided encryption key to use to server\-side encrypt the object in S3. If you provide this value, \fB\-\-sse\-c\fP must be specified as well. The key provided should \fBnot\fP be base64 encoded.
.sp
\fB\-\-sse\-kms\-key\-id\fP (string)
The customer\-managed AWS Key Management Service (KMS) key ID that should be used to server\-side encrypt the object in S3. You should only provide this parameter if you are using a customer managed customer master key (CMK) and not the AWS managed KMS CMK.
.sp
\fB\-\-sse\-c\-copy\-source\fP (string)
This parameter should only be specified when copying an S3 object that was encrypted server\-side with a customer\-provided key. It specifies the algorithm to use when decrypting the source object. \fBAES256\fP is the only valid value. If the parameter is specified but no value is provided, \fBAES256\fP is used. If you provide this value, \fB\-\-sse\-c\-copy\-source\-key\fP must be specified as well.
.sp
\fB\-\-sse\-c\-copy\-source\-key\fP (blob)
This parameter should only be specified when copying an S3 object that was encrypted server\-side with a customer\-provided key. Specifies the customer\-provided encryption key for Amazon S3 to use to decrypt the source object. The encryption key provided must be one that was used when the source object was created. If you provide this value, \fB\-\-sse\-c\-copy\-source\fP be specified as well. The key provided should \fBnot\fP be base64 encoded.
.sp
\fB\-\-storage\-class\fP (string)
The type of storage to use for the object. Valid choices are: STANDARD | REDUCED_REDUNDANCY | STANDARD_IA | ONEZONE_IA | INTELLIGENT_TIERING | GLACIER | DEEP_ARCHIVE | GLACIER_IR. Defaults to \(aqSTANDARD\(aq
.sp
\fB\-\-grants\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Grant specific permissions to individual users or groups. You can supply a list of grants of the form
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
\-\-grants Permission=Grantee_Type=Grantee_ID [Permission=Grantee_Type=Grantee_ID ...]
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
To specify the same permission type for multiple grantees, specify the permission as such as
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
\-\-grants Permission=Grantee_Type=Grantee_ID,Grantee_Type=Grantee_ID,...
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Each value contains the following elements:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPermission\fP \- Specifies the granted permissions, and can be set to read, readacl, writeacl, or full.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGrantee_Type\fP \- Specifies how the grantee is to be identified, and can be set to uri or id.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGrantee_ID\fP \- Specifies the grantee based on Grantee_Type. The \fBGrantee_ID\fP value can be one of:
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBuri\fP \- The group\(aqs URI. For more information, see \fI\%Who Is a Grantee?\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBid\fP \- The account\(aqs canonical ID
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
For more information on Amazon S3 access control, see \fI\%Access Control\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-website\-redirect\fP (string)
If the bucket is configured as a website, redirects requests for this object to another object in the same bucket or to an external URL. Amazon S3 stores the value of this header in the object metadata.
.sp
\fB\-\-content\-type\fP (string)
Specify an explicit content type for this operation. This value overrides any guessed mime types.
.sp
\fB\-\-cache\-control\fP (string)
Specifies caching behavior along the request/reply chain.
.sp
\fB\-\-content\-disposition\fP (string)
Specifies presentational information for the object.
.sp
\fB\-\-content\-encoding\fP (string)
Specifies what content encodings have been applied to the object and thus what decoding mechanisms must be applied to obtain the media\-type referenced by the Content\-Type header field.
.sp
\fB\-\-content\-language\fP (string)
The language the content is in.
.sp
\fB\-\-expires\fP (string)
The date and time at which the object is no longer cacheable.
.sp
\fB\-\-source\-region\fP (string)
When transferring objects from an s3 bucket to an s3 bucket, this specifies the region of the source bucket. Note the region specified by \fB\-\-region\fP or through configuration of the CLI refers to the region of the destination bucket. If \fB\-\-source\-region\fP is not specified the region of the source will be the same as the region of the destination bucket.
.sp
\fB\-\-only\-show\-errors\fP (boolean)
Only errors and warnings are displayed. All other output is suppressed.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fP (boolean)
File transfer progress is not displayed. This flag is only applied when the quiet and only\-show\-errors flags are not provided.
.sp
\fB\-\-progress\-frequency\fP (integer)
Number of seconds to wait before updating file transfer progress. This flag is only applied when the quiet and only\-show\-errors flags are not provided.
.sp
\fB\-\-progress\-multiline\fP (boolean)
Show progress on multiple lines.
.sp
\fB\-\-page\-size\fP (integer)
The number of results to return in each response to a list operation. The default value is 1000 (the maximum allowed). Using a lower value may help if an operation times out.
.sp
\fB\-\-ignore\-glacier\-warnings\fP (boolean)
Turns off glacier warnings. Warnings about an operation that cannot be performed because it involves copying, downloading, or moving a glacier object will no longer be printed to standard error and will no longer cause the return code of the command to be \fB2\fP\&.
.sp
\fB\-\-force\-glacier\-transfer\fP (boolean)
Forces a transfer request on all Glacier objects in a sync or recursive copy.
.sp
\fB\-\-request\-payer\fP (string)
Confirms that the requester knows that they will be charged for the request. Bucket owners need not specify this parameter in their requests. Documentation on downloading objects from requester pays buckets can be found at \fI\%http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/ObjectsinRequesterPaysBuckets.html\fP
.sp
\fB\-\-checksum\-mode\fP (string)
To retrieve the checksum, this mode must be enabled. If the object has a checksum, it will be verified.
.sp
\fB\-\-checksum\-algorithm\fP (string)
Indicates the algorithm used to create the checksum for the object.
.sp
\fB\-\-metadata\fP (map)
A map of metadata to store with the objects in S3. This will be applied to every object which is part of this request. In a sync, this means that files which haven\(aqt changed won\(aqt receive the new metadata. key \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
value \-> (string)
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Shorthand Syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
KeyName1=string,KeyName2=string
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
JSON Syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
{\(dqstring\(dq: \(dqstring\(dq
  ...}
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-copy\-props\fP (string)
Determines which properties are copied from the source S3 object. This parameter only applies for S3 to S3 copies. Valid values are:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnone\fP \- Do not copy any of the properties from the source S3 object.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmetadata\-directive\fP \- Copies the following properties from the source S3 object: \fBcontent\-type\fP, \fBcontent\-language\fP, \fBcontent\-encoding\fP, \fBcontent\-disposition\fP, \fBcache\-control\fP, \fB\-\-expires\fP, and \fBmetadata\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdefault\fP \- The default value. Copies tags and properties covered under the \fBmetadata\-directive\fP value from the source S3 object.
.UNINDENT
.sp
In order to copy the appropriate properties for multipart copies, some of the options may require additional API calls if a multipart copy is involved. Specifically:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmetadata\-directive\fP may require additional \fBHeadObject\fP API calls.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdefault\fP may require additional \fBHeadObject\fP, \fBGetObjectTagging\fP, and \fBPutObjectTagging\fP API calls. Note this list of API calls may grow in the future in order to ensure multipart copies preserve the exact properties a \fBCopyObject\fP API call would preserve.
.UNINDENT
.sp
If you want to guarantee no additional API calls are made other than than the ones needed to perform the actual copy, set this option to \fBnone\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-metadata\-directive\fP (string)
Sets the \fBx\-amz\-metadata\-directive\fP header for CopyObject operations. It is recommended to use the \fB\-\-copy\-props\fP parameter instead to control copying of metadata properties. If \fB\-\-metadata\-directive\fP is set, the \fB\-\-copy\-props\fP parameter will be disabled and will have no affect on the transfer.
.sp
\fB\-\-recursive\fP (boolean)
Command is performed on all files or objects under the specified directory or prefix.
.sp
\fB\-\-validate\-same\-s3\-paths\fP (boolean)
Resolves the source and destination S3 URIs to their underlying buckets and verifies that the file or object is not being moved onto itself. If you are using any type of access point ARNs or access point aliases in your S3 URIs, we strongly recommended using this parameter to help prevent accidental deletions of the source file or object. This parameter resolves the underlying buckets of S3 access point ARNs and aliases, S3 on Outposts access point ARNs, and Multi\-Region Access Point ARNs. S3 on Outposts access point aliases are not supported. Instead of using this parameter, you can set the environment variable \fBAWS_CLI_S3_MV_VALIDATE_SAME_S3_PATHS\fP to \fBtrue\fP\&. NOTE: Path validation requires making additional API calls. Future updates to this path\-validation mechanism might change which API calls are made.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-debug\fP (boolean)
.sp
Turn on debug logging.
.sp
\fB\-\-endpoint\-url\fP (string)
.sp
Override command\(aqs default URL with the given URL.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-verify\-ssl\fP (boolean)
.sp
By default, the AWS CLI uses SSL when communicating with AWS services. For each SSL connection, the AWS CLI will verify SSL certificates. This option overrides the default behavior of verifying SSL certificates.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-paginate\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable automatic pagination. If automatic pagination is disabled, the AWS CLI will only make one call, for the first page of results.
.sp
\fB\-\-output\fP (string)
.sp
The formatting style for command output.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
text
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
yaml
.IP \(bu 2
yaml\-stream
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-query\fP (string)
.sp
A JMESPath query to use in filtering the response data.
.sp
\fB\-\-profile\fP (string)
.sp
Use a specific profile from your credential file.
.sp
\fB\-\-region\fP (string)
.sp
The region to use. Overrides config/env settings.
.sp
\fB\-\-version\fP (string)
.sp
Display the version of this tool.
.sp
\fB\-\-color\fP (string)
.sp
Turn on/off color output.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-sign\-request\fP (boolean)
.sp
Do not sign requests. Credentials will not be loaded if this argument is provided.
.sp
\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fP (string)
.sp
The CA certificate bundle to use when verifying SSL certificates. Overrides config/env settings.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-read\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket read time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket read will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket connect time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket connect will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-binary\-format\fP (string)
.sp
The formatting style to be used for binary blobs. The default format is base64. The base64 format expects binary blobs to be provided as a base64 encoded string. The raw\-in\-base64\-out format preserves compatibility with AWS CLI V1 behavior and binary values must be passed literally. When providing contents from a file that map to a binary blob \fBfileb://\fP will always be treated as binary and use the file contents directly regardless of the \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP setting. When using \fBfile://\fP the file contents will need to properly formatted for the configured \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
base64
.IP \(bu 2
raw\-in\-base64\-out
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-pager\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable cli pager for output.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
To use the following examples, you must have the AWS CLI installed and configured. See the \fI\%Getting started guide\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP for more information.
.sp
Unless otherwise stated, all examples have unix\-like quotation rules. These examples will need to be adapted to your terminal\(aqs quoting rules. See \fI\%Using quotation marks with strings\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 1: Move a local file to the specified bucket\fP
.sp
The following \fBmv\fP command moves a single file to a specified bucket and key.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv test.txt s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test2.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: test.txt to s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test2.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 2: Move an object to the specified bucket and key\fP
.sp
The following \fBmv\fP command moves a single s3 object to a specified bucket and key.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test.txt s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test2.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test.txt to s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test2.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 3: Move an S3 object to the local directory\fP
.sp
The following \fBmv\fP command moves a single object to a specified file locally.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test.txt test2.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test.txt to test2.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 4: Move an object with it\(aqs original name to the specified bucket\fP
.sp
The following \fBmv\fP command moves a single object to a specified bucket while retaining its original name:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test.txt s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket2/
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test.txt to s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket2/test.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 5: Move all objects and prefixes in a bucket to the local directory\fP
.sp
When passed with the parameter \fB\-\-recursive\fP, the following \fBmv\fP command recursively moves all objects under a
specified prefix and bucket to a specified directory.  In this example, the bucket \fBamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\fP has the objects
\fBtest1.txt\fP and \fBtest2.txt\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket . \e
    \-\-recursive
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test1.txt to test1.txt
move: s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test2.txt to test2.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 6: Move all objects and prefixes in a bucket to the local directory, except \(ga\(ga.jpg\(ga\(ga files\fP
.sp
When passed with the parameter \fB\-\-recursive\fP, the following \fBmv\fP command recursively moves all files under a
specified directory to a specified bucket and prefix while excluding some files by using an \fB\-\-exclude\fP parameter. In
this example, the directory \fBmyDir\fP has the files \fBtest1.txt\fP and \fBtest2.jpg\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv myDir s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/ \e
    \-\-recursive \e
    \-\-exclude \(dq*.jpg\(dq
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: myDir/test1.txt to s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket2/test1.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 7: Move all objects and prefixes in a bucket to the local directory, except specified prefix\fP
.sp
When passed with the parameter \fB\-\-recursive\fP, the following \fBmv\fP command recursively moves all objects under a
specified bucket to another bucket while excluding some objects by using an \fB\-\-exclude\fP parameter.  In this example,
the bucket \fBamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\fP has the objects \fBtest1.txt\fP and \fBanother/test1.txt\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/ s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket2/ \e
    \-\-recursive \e
    \-\-exclude \(dqamzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/another/*\(dq
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test1.txt to s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket2/test1.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 8: Move an object to the specified bucket and set the ACL\fP
.sp
The following \fBmv\fP command moves a single object to a specified bucket and key while setting the ACL to
\fBpublic\-read\-write\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test.txt s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test2.txt \e
    \-\-acl public\-read\-write
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test.txt to s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/test2.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 9: Move a local file to the specified bucket and grant permissions\fP
.sp
The following \fBmv\fP command illustrates the use of the \fB\-\-grants\fP option to grant read access to all users and full
control to a specific user identified by their email address.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv file.txt s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/ \e
    \-\-grants read=uri=http://acs.amazonaws.com/groups/global/AllUsers full=emailaddress=user@example.com
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: file.txt to s3://amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket/file.txt
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBExample 10: Move a file to an S3 access point\fP
.sp
The following \fBmv\fP command moves a single file named \fBmydoc.txt\fP to the access point named \fBmyaccesspoint\fP at the key named \fBmykey\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3 mv mydoc.txt s3://arn:aws:s3:us\-west\-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/mykey
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
move: mydoc.txt to s3://arn:aws:s3:us\-west\-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/mykey
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
